{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":301927,"name":"Thomas Kehrenberg","username":"tmk","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/tmk/{size}/10935_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T19:48:08.326Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eFor your consideration: \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0845/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePEP 845\u003c/a\u003e, with the following abstract:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis PEP enables the use of non-attribute names as \u003cstrong\u003evalue patterns\u003c/strong\u003e in match statements. A name prefixed with a dot is looked up using the normal name resolution rules and compared to the match subject by equality in the same manner as existing value patterns, instead of being treated as a \u003cstrong\u003ecapture pattern\u003c/strong\u003e. This makes it possible to match local variables and global variables defined in the same module without using a guard clause.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"python\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-python\"\u003edef get_book_titles_for_author(author: str):\n    for book in BOOKS:\n        match book:\n            case {\"title\": title, \"author\": .author}:\n                yield title\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can also try it out in the demo here: \u003ca href=\"https://pep845-demo.pages.dev/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://pep845-demo.pages.dev/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0845/\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/7/8/7808f673c94c5abc6cdd738548e39c7ae50dc418.png\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"979F6B\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0845/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePython Enhancement Proposals (PEPs)\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cimg width=\"200\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/8/e/8eb386d43fc93f43e4e34ee56dd1c3ebf682e66d.png\" class=\"thumbnail onebox-avatar\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"9EAC81\"\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0845/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePEP 845 – Leading-Dot Value Patterns | peps.python.org\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003eThis PEP enables the use of non-attribute names as value patterns in match statements. A name prefixed with a dot is looked up using the normal name resolution rules and compared to the match subject by equality in the same manner as existing value...\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T19:48:08.326Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":141,"reads":290,"readers_count":289,"score":1266.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":109100,"topic_slug":"pep-845-leading-dot-value-patterns","display_username":"Thomas Kehrenberg","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0845/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 845 – Leading-Dot Value Patterns | peps.python.org","clicks":119},{"url":"https://pep845-demo.pages.dev/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Python PEP 845 - Interactive Demo","clicks":20},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pattern-matching-on-constants-that-arent-in-a-namespace-especially-sentinels/107916/72","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Pattern matching on constants that aren't in a namespace (especially sentinels)","clicks":3},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-845-leading-dot-value-patterns-for-match-statement/109405","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"PEP 845: Leading-Dot Value Patterns for match statement","clicks":0},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-845-leading-dot-value-patterns-for-match-statement/109405/11","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"PEP 845: Leading-Dot Value Patterns for match statement","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":35}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":6709,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-845-leading-dot-value-patterns/109100/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":35}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":35,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":301954,"name":"Neil Girdhar","username":"NeilGirdhar","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/neilgirdhar/{size}/5776_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-18T00:56:44.485Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eCool idea!  Is \u003ccode\u003eLiteral[author]\u003c/code\u003e possible?  Or does that violate \u003ccode\u003eLiteral\u003c/code\u003e’s normal usage too much?  Feel free to add it to rejected ideas.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-09-18T01:28:04.033Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":257,"readers_count":256,"score":60.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":109100,"topic_slug":"pep-845-leading-dot-value-patterns","display_username":"Neil Girdhar","primary_group_name":null,"fla